uuid": "1ATVCkzkum", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 13, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "kek", "id": 8821780, "raw_content": "", "author": "journalist", "created": 1788788135687, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "grenades_and_ham", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.breitbart.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVCkzkum.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.breitbart.com/middle-east/2026/09/05/palestinian-journalist-calls-hakeem-jeffries-a-monkey-and-errand-boy/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Palestinian Journalist Calls Hakeem Jeffries a \u2018Monkey\u2019 and \u2018Errand Boy\u2019", "last_comment_created": 1788790698610, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 13, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A Palestinian journalist blew right through the forbidden red line of African American racist terms by referring to black House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries (D-NY) as a \u201cmonkey\u201d and a \u201cboy.\" | Israel / Middle East", "large_image": "hRyN4iys9a6ikBsj.png", "title": "Palestinian Journalist Calls Hakeem Jeffries a 'Monkey' and 'Errand Boy'"}, "post_flair_text": "\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0TOP\u00a0\u00a0KEK\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVCkzkqm", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 13, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8821778, "raw_content": "I keep seeing this argument. \"If Lindsay Clancy is acquitted because of insanity from woman hormones, this means we'll have legal precedent for saying that women cannot be trust with things like political power and responsibility. This will actually be a fatal blow to feminism\".\n\nI'm sorry, but that is a cope and it is patently absurd and nonsensical. Because it relies on something being true that most certainly is not true. It presumes the Left gives one flying fuck about universally, rationally, and evenly applied standards. \n\nHere's how it'll play out in real life.\n\nThe Left gets Clancy off because of woman hormones and emotions. The Right then says \"Aha! You admitted a woman can be so emotional that she can't control her actions and that they can't be trusted to weild power, authority, and responsibility because of that. Checkmate feminists, you backed yourself into a corner and now you have to apply that standard to yourself\"\n\nAnd the Left will simply say \"No. We don't care about hypocrisy. That's *your* moral standard, not ours. We're going to keep letting women get off the hook when it suits us, but simultaneously continue to give them power and authority when that suits us.\n\nWe'll call them hypocrites, and they'll say so the fuck what, what are you going to do about it? Be mad on the internet and make some memes?\n\nAnd then we'll hit the same impasse we've hit 10,000 other times when we call them hypocrites over something and they smirk and say who cares. We never have a next step in mind. Because being called out for being a hypocrite would work on *us*, and we would change our behavior to fix the moral lapse, we foolishly assume that weapon works against everyone. It doesn't of course, it has never worked on the Left and never will. They will never change their behavior because we called them out for being immoral or hypocritical. They will have to be *forced*. And since we don't do that, we'll be stuck spluttering and spinning our wheels here too just like we do every other time. \n\nThe feminists will just say \"No. We're not applying this back on ourselves.\" And we'll have nothing left to say or do about it. \n\nThe fatal flaw of the Right is that we are stuck on this eternal quest to find the perfect rational and reasonable well-articulated and factually proven rhetorical and logical argument that will demolish and undo the Left. Except the Left just does not give even one fuck about rational arguments or well articulated logic. We keep attacking them with weapons that have utterly no meaning or effect to them, and continually get flabbergasted when it doesn't work. ", "author": "SmiggieBalls", "created": 1788788044764, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Stop saying Lindsay Clancy getting off because of hormones will be a good thing in the long run", "last_comment_created": 1788788044764, "content": "<p>I keep seeing this argument. &quot;If Lindsay Clancy is acquitted because of insanity from woman hormones, this means we'll have legal precedent for saying that women cannot be trust with things like political power and responsibility. This will actually be a fatal blow to feminism&quot;.</p>\n<p>I'm sorry, but that is a cope and it is patently absurd and nonsensical. Because it relies on something being true that most certainly is not true. It presumes the Left gives one flying fuck about universally, rationally, and evenly applied standards.</p>\n<p>Here's how it'll play out in real life.</p>\n<p>The Left gets Clancy off because of woman hormones and emotions. The Right then says &quot;Aha! You admitted a woman can be so emotional that she can't control her actions and that they can't be trusted to weild power, authority, and responsibility because of that. Checkmate feminists, you backed yourself into a corner and now you have to apply that standard to yourself&quot;</p>\n<p>And the Left will simply say &quot;No. We don't care about hypocrisy. That's <em>your</em> moral standard, not ours. We're going to keep letting women get off the hook when it suits us, but simultaneously continue to give them power and authority when that suits us.</p>\n<p>We'll call them hypocrites, and they'll say so the fuck what, what are you going to do about it? Be mad on the internet and make some memes?</p>\n<p>And then we'll hit the same impasse we've hit 10,000 other times when we call them hypocrites over something and they smirk and say who cares. We never have a next step in mind. Because being called out for being a hypocrite would work on <em>us</em>, and we would change our behavior to fix the moral lapse, we foolishly assume that weapon works against everyone. It doesn't of course, it has never worked on the Left and never will. They will never change their behavior because we called them out for being immoral or hypocritical. They will have to be <em>forced</em>. And since we don't do that, we'll be stuck spluttering and spinning our wheels here too just like we do every other time.</p>\n<p>The feminists will just say &quot;No. We're not applying this back on ourselves.&quot; And we'll have nothing left to say or do about it.</p>\n<p>The fatal flaw of the Right is that we are stuck on this eternal quest to find the perfect rational and reasonable well-articulated and factually proven rhetorical and logical argument that will demolish and undo the Left. Except the Left just does not give even one fuck about rational arguments or well articulated logic. We keep attacking them with weapons that have utterly no meaning or effect to them, and continually get flabbergasted when it doesn't work.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 13, "is_edited": true, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVCl0IXy", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 9, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8821912, "raw_content": "", "author": "cyberrigger", "created": 1788795235401, "profile_picture": "0UVsiKsLavnh", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "DITTOPatriot", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVCl0IXy.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/nGqhm2FG6teT.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/SqxK5oZtxlZzRay9.png", "width": 577, "content-type": "png", "height": 768}], "blurhash": "U9Lz:SRjIb?a00t70gM{00WB%1Rk01jZ~Uxt", "full_resolution": [1798, 1350]}, "title": "The Arch of Fiat Currency was paid for by devaluing the dollar in your wallet", "last_comment_created": 1788799602515, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 2, "score_up": 9, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVCl0ITw", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 9, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8821908, "raw_content": "", "author": "whatremainsanymore", "created": 1788795086544, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author"